ce-nowrap">$140 + $120</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right font-bold text-white whitespace-nowrap">$260</td></tr><tr class="odd:bg-slate-950 even:bg-slate-900/40"><td class="px-4 py-3 whitespace-nowrap text-white">30 miles</td><td class="px-4 py-3">Spokane to Coeur d’Alene<span class="block sm:hidden text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1">$140 + $180</span></td><td class="px-4 py-3 hidden sm:table-cell whitespace-nowrap">$140 + $180</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right font-bold text-white whitespace-nowrap">$320</td></tr><tr class="odd:bg-slate-950 even:bg-slate-900/40"><td class="px-4 py-3 whitespace-nowrap text-white">50 miles</td><td class="px-4 py-3">Spokane to a rural shop out of the metro<span class="block sm:hidden text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1">$140 + $300</span></td><td class="px-4 py-3 hidden sm:table-cell whitespace-nowrap">$140 + $300</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right font-bold text-white whitespace-nowrap">$440</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">Distances above are rough road miles. For your exact route, use the <a class="text-red-500 font-semibold hover:underline" href="/quote">instant towing quote calculator</a>; it measures the drive between your pickup and drop-off.</p><h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-14 mb-5 pt-10 border-t border-slate-800">What can make a tow cost more</h2><p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">The hook-plus-mileage estimate covers a normal tow of a car, SUV or light truck that is on or next to the road. These situations are quoted separately, and the price is still confirmed before dispatch:</p><div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 my-6"><div class="border border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-5"><p class="font-semibold text-white mb-1">Winch-outs and recoveries.</p><p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">A car in a ditch, snowbank or mud needs to be pulled out before it can be towed. See <a class="text-red-500 font-semibold hover:underline" href="/winch-out-recovery">winch out and recovery</a>.</p></div><div class="border border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-5"><p class="font-semibold text-white mb-1">Heavy vehicles.</p><p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">Box trucks, RVs, buses and equipment need a larger truck. See <a class="text-red-500 font-semibold hover:underline" href="/heavy-duty-towing">heavy duty towing</a>.</p></div><div class="border border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-5"><p class="font-semibold text-white mb-1">Accident scenes.</p><p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">Debris cleanup, wheels that will not roll, or a car that needs dollies. See <a class="text-red-500 font-semibold hover:underline" href="/accident-towing-spokane">accident towing in Spokane</a>.</p></div><div class="border border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-5"><p class="font-semibold text-white mb-1">Long trips.</p><p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">Tows to another city or state are usually quoted as a flat rate. See <a class="text-red-500 font-semibold hover:underline" href="/long-distance-towing">long distance towing</a>.</p></div></div><div class="bg-slate-900/70 border border-slate-800 border-l-4 border-l-red-500/60 rounded-lg p-5 my-6 text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">A flatbed, which many AWD, lowered and luxury cars need, does not by itself change the estimate. Just mention the vehicle when you call so the right truck is sent. More on that on the <a class="text-red-500 font-semibold hover:underline" href="/flatbed-towing">flatbed towing</a> page.</div><div class="my-12 border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/70 rounded-xl p-6 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4"><div class="text-center sm:text-left"><p class="text-lg font-semibold text-white">Want your exact price?</p><p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Call and get the total before a truck is sent.</p></div><a href="tel:+15097977999" class="shrink-0 bg-gradient-to-r from-red-600 to-red-700 text-white px-6 py-3 rounded-xl hover:from-red-700 hover:to-red-800 transition font-semibold flex items-center gap-2"><svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M3 5a2 2 0 012-2h3.28a1 1 0 01.948.684l1.498 4.493a1 1 0 01-.502 1.21l-2.257 1.13a11.042 11.042 0 005.516 5.516l1.13-2.257a1 1 0 011.21-.502l4.493 1.498a1 1 0 01.684.949V19a2 2 0 01-2 2h-1C9.716 21 3 14.284 3 6V5z"></path></svg><span>(509) 797-7999</span></a></div><h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-0 mb-5 pt-10 border-t border-slate-800">How to keep your towing bill down</h2><ul class="space-y-2 my-6"><li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="shrink-0 mt-1 text-red-400"><svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg></span><span class="text-gray-300"><strong class="text-white">Pick the closest good shop.</strong> Every extra mile is $6. A shop 5 miles away instead of 20 saves about $60.</span></li><li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="shrink-0 mt-1 text-red-400"><svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg></span><span class="text-gray-300"><strong class="text-white">Check if you even need a tow.</strong> A dead battery, flat tire or lockout can often be fixed where you are. See <a class="text-red-500 font-semibold hover:underline" href="/battery-jump-start">jump starts</a> and <a class="text-red-500 font-semibold hover:underline" href="/lockout-flat-tire">lockout and flat tire help</a>.</span></li><li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="shrink-0 mt-1 text-red-400"><svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg></span><span class="text-gray-300"><strong class="text-white">Check your insurance and card benefits.</strong> Many auto policies, new-car warranties and some credit cards include towing coverage or reimbursement. Ask for an itemized receipt so you can submit it.</span></li><li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="shrink-0 mt-1 text-red-400"><svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg></span><span class="text-gray-300"><strong class="text-white">Call before it gets worse.</strong> A car stopped on the shoulder is a simple tow. The same car slid into a ditch overnight needs a recovery, which costs more.</span></li><li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="shrink-0 mt-1 text-red-400"><svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg></span><span class="text-gray-300"><strong class="text-white">Get the price first.</strong> Always ask for the total before a truck is sent. We give you that number on the phone.</span></li></ul><h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-14 mb-5 pt-10 border-t border-slate-800">Cheap towing in Spokane without surprises</h2><div class="bg-slate-900/70 border border-slate-800 border-l-4 border-l-amber-500/70 rounded-lg p-5 my-6 text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">The cheapest-sounding quote is not always the cheapest tow. Watch for low prices that leave out mileage, &quot;after-hours&quot; add-ons, or storage charges that start the moment your car reaches a yard.</div><p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">With a flat $140 hook fee, $6 per mile and a $200 minimum, you can work out the cost yourself before you call. If your car was towed by someone else, such as from a private lot or by police order, that is a different situation with different fees; see <a class="text-red-500 font-semibold hover:underline" href="/towed-car-spokane">what to do if your car was towed in Spokane</a>.</p><p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">For everything else we can help with across the region, see <a class="text-red-500 font-semibold hover:underline" href="/spokane-towing-services">Spokane towing services</a>.</p><h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-14 mb-5 pt-10 border-t border-slate-800">Frequently Asked Questions</h2><div class="divide-y divide-slate-800 border-y border-slate-800"><div class="py-5"><h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-2">How much does a tow cost in Spokane?</h3><p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">Online estimates use a $140 hook fee plus $6 per mile, with a $200 minimum. Most tows inside Spokane are under 10 miles and cost $200. A 15-mile tow is about $230 and a 30-mile tow (Spokane to Coeur d’Alene) is about $320. The exact price is confirmed on the phone before a truck is sent.</p></div><div class="py-5"><h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-2">How much does towing cost per mile?</h3><p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">Mileage is $6 per mile from pickup to drop-off, on top of the $140 hook fee. The $200 minimum means tows of about 10 miles or less all cost $200.</p></div><div class="py-5"><h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-2">Is there a cheaper option than a tow?</h3><p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">Sometimes. If the problem is a dead battery, a flat tire or keys locked inside, roadside help where the car sits is usually cheaper than towing it. Tell the dispatcher what happened and they will suggest the right service.</p></div><div class="py-5"><h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-2">Does insurance cover towing?</h3><p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">Many auto policies include roadside or towing coverage, and collision coverage often pays for towing after an accident. Coverage varies, so check your policy and keep the itemized receipt to submit for reimbursement.</p></div><div class="py-5"><h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-2">Do you charge extra at night or on weekends?</h3><p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">The estimate method is the same day or night: $140 hook fee plus $6 per mile, $200 minimum. Winch-outs, heavy vehicles and difficult recoveries are quoted separately, and you always get the price before dispatch.</p></div></div><div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-red-600 to-red-700 rounded-2xl p-8 text-center mt-12"><h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-white">Get Your Exact Towing Price</h3><p class="mb-6 text-white/90">Tell us where the car is and where it is going. You get the price before dispatch.</p><a href="tel:+15097977999" class="bg-white text-red-600 px-8 py-4 rounded-xl hover:bg-gray-100 transition font-bold text-lg inline-block shadow-lg">Call (509) 797-7999</a></div>
